# Review ownership for the harness itself. SECURITY.md names CODEOWNERS review as
# one of the three backstops behind the guard hooks (the others being CI parity via
# `tools/validate.mjs --min-floor` and manifest hashing via `doctor`) — the guards
# are tamper-EVIDENT, not tamper-proof, so the human review of a widening is the
# thing that actually holds.
#
# The scaffold ships its own CODEOWNERS to consumers from
# template/base/github/CODEOWNERS, parameterised by {{SECURITY_OWNERS}}. This file
# governs THIS repository.

*                                   @BhodiSea

# The enforcement surface. A change here can silently widen what an agent is
# allowed to do, in every downstream install, so it never rides along in a
# large diff unreviewed.
/scripts/                           @BhodiSea
/template/base/tools/               @BhodiSea
/template/base/.claude/hooks/       @BhodiSea
/template/base/eslint.config.mjs    @BhodiSea
/template/base/dependency-cruiser.cjs @BhodiSea

# Escape hatches: every file here EXEMPTS something from a gate or raises a
# budget. check-gate-integrity refuses to let them be modified-but-uncommitted
# precisely so the widening shows up in a reviewed diff.
/template/base/tools/*-allow.json   @BhodiSea
/template/base/tools/*-exempt.json  @BhodiSea
/template/base/tools/*-budget.json  @BhodiSea

# Supply chain and release.
/.github/workflows/                 @BhodiSea
/renovate.json                      @BhodiSea
/package.json                       @BhodiSea
